-- title:
--   Residual Tₚ-eigenvalue as Frobenius trace on inertia coinvariants
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $N \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N$, and let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \notin S_0$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring that is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, and assume $p$ lies in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $k$ be a field, $\psi : k \to \operatorname{ResidueField} \mathcal{O}'$ a ring homomorphism, and $\bar\rho$ a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a multiplicative map $\bar\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no Galois-stable submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals and assume the congruence condition: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$, $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $Q$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $Q$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $Q$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $Q$ as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ pushed forward along $\psi$ equals $X^2 - \overline{\chi(T_\ell)}X + \ell$. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, suppose some $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the image in $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) has $\bar\rho(\tau) \neq 1$, let $\sigma$ be a Frobenius element at $p$ for $P$ in the above sense, and let $E$ be a $k$-linear endomorphism of the inertia coinvariants $V / \sum_{\tau \in I_P} \operatorname{range}(\bar\rho(\tau) - 1)$ induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$, i.e. $E(\bar v) = \overline{\bar\rho(\sigma)v}$ for all $v \in V$. Then $\psi(\operatorname{tr}_k E)$ equals the image of $\chi(T_p)$ in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$.
--
--   This is the $T_p$ case, for $p$ odd and not dividing the level, of the local comparison at $p$ between the Hecke eigenvalues of a point of the weight-two Hecke algebra and the residual Galois representation attached to it (as in the analysis behind Lemma 4.6 of Darmon–Diamond–Taylor), here in the ramified situation where inertia at $P$ acts nontrivially. It feeds the construction of homomorphisms out of Hecke algebras prescribing Frobenius characteristic polynomials, via [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_extension_residue_eq_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_extension_residue_eq_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq) and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_ringHom_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq), and the congruence [`CohCarrier.heckeT_sub_algebraMap_mem_of_isMaximal_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CohCarrier.heckeT_sub_algebraMap_mem_of_isMaximal_of_not_dvd).
